1.  TWO FURTHEST HOUSES WITH DIFFERENT COLORS
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Q1. There are n houses evenly lined up on the street, and each house is beautifully painted. You are given a 0-indexed integer array colors of length n, where colors[i] represents the color of the ith house.
Return the maximum distance between two houses with different colors.
The distance between the ith and jth houses is abs(i - j), where abs(x) is the absolute value of x.

Sol.

class Solution {
    public int maxDistance(int[] colors) {
       int n = colors.length - 1;
       int ans = n ;
       int temp = 0 ;
        
        for(int i = 0 ; i <= n/2 ; i++){
		        if(colors[i] == colors[n-i] && colors[i] == colors[i+1] && colors[n-i] == colors[n-i-1]){
                temp = i;
                ans = n-temp-2;
		        }

            else if(colors[i] == colors[n-i] && i == 0){
                return n-1;
            }

            else{
                return ans;
            }
	    }
	   return ans;

    
